// SUBJECT NOTE — Frontier & Philosophy:
//   - The philosophy of religion: questions of God/the divine, faith, doubt, the sacred, the
//     classic arguments, the problem of evil, the relationship of faith and reason, and what
//     religion DOES in human life. Builds on L01 (metaphysics), L11 (mind/spiritual dimension
//     handled evenhandedly), L13/L14 (wisdom & ways of knowing).
//   - MAXIMUM EVENHANDEDNESS (calibration-critical): this is among the most personal, contested
//     topics there is. Treat believers AND non-believers with full respect; present the strongest
//     case for theism, for atheism, and for agnosticism; do NOT push any conclusion; explicitly
//     affirm that thoughtful, good people land in all these places. Respect that many families
//     (very plausibly the user's own, given a Catholic-influenced Latin American background) hold
//     sincere faith — the lesson must be a help to a believing family, not a solvent. Equally it
//     must respect non-believing and questioning kids. The stance: these are real, hard, open
//     questions humans have wrestled with forever, and the lesson teaches how to think and talk
//     about them well, not what to conclude.
//   - PROTECTIVE BACKBONE (carefully two-sided): (1) Guard against manipulation that uses
//     religious authority/garb — coercive control, predatory "prophets," cults, fear-based
//     control, financial exploitation ("give to be blessed"), us-vs-them weaponization. (2) BUT
//     do this WITHOUT smearing sincere faith or implying religion = manipulation; the test is the
//     same band-wide manipulation test (fear, isolation, unquestionable authority, money, control)
//     applied regardless of whether the wrapper is religious, political, wellness, or commercial.
//     Sincere faith communities and predatory cults are different things, and the lesson says so.
//   - Honesty tiers 3-4 (existence of God is tier-4 open). Em-dashes natural; do NOT replace.
//
// Interaction format: PERSPECTIVES (screen 7). 5 voices. Standard <Perspectives /> contract.
//
// QUIZ STANDARD (locked): 8 MC + 1 TF + 1 inference. Short ~1-line options, comparable length,
// plausible misconception distractors, correct rotated/not-longest; teaching in `explanation`.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

