              explanation: `The relationship is genuinely complex, not the cartoon battle loud voices present. Many of the deepest religious thinkers were brilliant reasoners who used rigorous argument in service of faith; many great scientists have been religious; and many thoughtful people conclude reason leads them away from belief. Also, "faith" itself means different things — sometimes belief without evidence (fair to question), but often trust/commitment beyond what proof can establish, which everyone does in some form.`,
